**Main Takeaway**  
> 2-3 sentences explaining impact, trend, or why it matters.

---
```

### 5 — Smart Length Control

* If a listicle or event-blast has **> 10 items**:

  * Show first 10, then add “…and **N more** ➡️” (link back to newsletter).
* If it has **< 3 items**, auto-expand bullets with brief context so each has ≥ 8 words.

### 6 — Calendar Hooks

For every bullet that contains a **date + location**, append `📅 Add to Calendar` with an auto-generated `.ics` link:

```
BEGIN:VCALENDAR
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20250621T230000Z
SUMMARY:Event Name
LOCATION:Venue
DESCRIPTION:[Newsletter Title]
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
```

Provide the `.ics` as a data-URI or attach per your platform’s capability.

### 7 — Accessibility

* Use each image’s `alt` attribute; if it’s > 140 chars, shorten sensibly.
* Supply **plain-text fallback** after the digest:

```
---
Plain-Text Fallback
===================
[strip all Markdown formatting here]
```

### 8 — Trending Now

After all sections and before the fallback, include:

```
### 🔍 Trending Now
• 📈 [Keyword] ↑ (mentions +3 since yesterday)  
• 📉 [Keyword] ↓
```

Count keyword frequency across today’s JSON vs. the 7-day cache (exclude stop-words).

### 9 — Error Surfacing

At bottom, add hidden comments:

```
<!-- SKIPPED_TOTAL: X promos, Y duplicates -->
<!-- PARSE_ERRORS: 0 -->
```

Keep no other commentary.

### 10 — Output

Return **Markdown only** (no code fences, no HTML).
Hidden HTML comments (`<!-- ... -->`) are allowed for debug data.

